    <MESSAGE value="  • New service view (viewService) with three panels:                                                                                                                                                                              &#10;       • Configuration — app (link), delivery method, deploy target, delivery route, plus actions: Edit service, Service config (deploy target modal, same as before), and Remove                                                   &#10;       • Deployed in — every deployment of the app with this service's pinned version per env (Dev/UAT/Prod) and status dots; rows link into the deployment view                                                                    &#10;       • Secrets &amp; variables — service level — the existing level panel with inheritance (client → project → app → service) and + Variable / + Secret buttons                                                                       &#10;   • Navigation: service rows in the Services list now go to the service screen (the app name in the row still links to the app); service names in the app view are links too. Breadcrumb: Services / &lt;app&gt; / &lt;service&gt;, sidebar    &#10;     highlights Services, and a stale selection falls back gracefully after refresh.                                                                                                                                                &#10;   • Edit service: openServiceModal now supports edit mode — prefilled fields, saves via updateDoc('Sebrus Service', …) instead of create." />
    <MESSAGE value="&quot;Replace 'Retry Deploy' with unified 'Deploy' action&quot;&#10;&#10;Simplify deployment actions by replacing the &quot;Retry Deploy&quot; and &quot;Mark Deployed&quot; steps with a single unified &quot;Deploy&quot; action. The updated workflow adjusts approval handling based on environments and clarifies roles, ensuring seamless transitions and reducing complexity for deployment scenarios." />
    <MESSAGE value="&quot;Add commit resolution for services without linked repositories&quot;&#10;&#10;Introduce `find_commit_project` API to locate the Integration Project from a commit SHA. Update deployment modal to resolve repositories using pinned image versions when no repo link is provided, enhancing change history access for services." />
